  "notes": "{裂|さ}く means to tear or split something apart by force.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{裂|さ}ける→裂ける：02283_sakeru⟧ (intransitive, to be torn/split)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{紙|かみ}→紙：00712_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{裂|さ}く: to tear paper\n- ⟦{布|ぬの}→布：01489_nuno⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{裂|さ}く: to rip cloth\n- ⟦{二人|ふたり}→二人：00622_futari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{裂|さ}く: to separate two people (figurative)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {裂|さ}く: to tear, rip\n- ⟦{咲|さ}く→咲く：08150_saku⟧: to bloom (flowers) — same pronunciation, different meaning\n- ⟦{割|さ}く→割く：11820_saku⟧: to spare (time/resources) — different kanji, same pronunciation",
